# EigenScript#1102 (found closing ouroboros#106): a user-defined `report` is
# half-shadowed on the VM -- `report of <ident>` still compiles to the observer
# op, `report of <expr>` calls the user function. Pinned here so the
# self-hosted compiler stays byte-exact with the VM; when EigenScript decides
# the contract, this program changes on both sides at the next pin bump.
define report(v) as:
    return "mine"
x is 1
x is 2
print of (report of x)
print of (report of 5)
print of (report of (x + 0))
